// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
//
// Studio SegmentationService surface — Segmentation epic (Issue #1775).
//
// Manages per-(org, user) segmentation runs. The CRUD surface
// (CreateSegmentation / GetSegmentation / ListSegmentations /
// DeleteSegmentation) goes LIVE in T2, joined by the synchronous, draft-only
// ExtractAudienceFromDocument in T5 and by SuggestSplit in T8/T9 (split
// suggestion + operator override, #1781 / #1782); the generate/refine surface
// (GenerateSegments / RenameSegment / RegenerateSegment / LockSegment /
// ReweightSegment) is fully defined here for contract stability but stays
// UNIMPLEMENTED until the generation/refine tickets after T9 land.
//
// CreateSegmentation writes a status="draft" domain row synchronously.
// DeleteSegmentation removes a row. SuggestSplit UPDATEs the split columns of
// an existing row. All three are state-changing and owe the full
// audit-emission contract: state-changing RPCs write their domain event + audit
// twin to the outbox in the same tx as the domain write (CONVENTIONS §2; never
// a direct NATS publish from a handler). Reads (GetSegmentation /
// ListSegmentations) and the ephemeral ExtractAudienceFromDocument emit no
// events.
//
// Event subjects (svc emits — paired 1:1 with their audit twins per
// CONVENTIONS §2; the audit twin joins entity and action with an underscore,
// which is the form studio_svc.audit.subjects.audit_subject() produces):
//
//   business (each paired with its audit twin):
//     studio.segmentation.created.<org_id>          ↔ audit.studio.segmentation_created
//     studio.segmentation.deleted.<org_id>          ↔ audit.studio.segmentation_deleted
//     studio.segmentation.split_suggested.<org_id>  ↔ audit.studio.segmentation_split_suggested
//
// split_suggested (T8) is a genuinely NEW kind of state change, not a re-use of
// created/deleted: it mutates an existing run's resolved_split /
// recommended_count rather than creating or removing a row. A T9 re-propose
// overwrites those columns again and emits split_suggested again — expected,
// not an error. Each business subject must also be registered in
// eventbus.EventsStreamSubjects (platform/libs/go/eventbus/stream.go) in the
// exact form it is published: a subject outside the EVENTS stream allowlist is
// rejected with "no response from stream" and leaves an undrainable row that
// head-of-line-blocks the SHARED studio-svc outbox drainer.
//
// The async lifecycle subjects (generating / ready / error), the worker
// job-dispatch subject, and the per-job job_progress subject are NOT declared
// yet — they are added by the generation tickets when GenerateSegments / the
// refine RPCs go live and enqueue worker jobs. SuggestSplit itself is
// synchronous and enqueues no worker job.

